he status endpoint reports the branch run as passed.", "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 376439, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Ea6piF3ZQ4xnVeJdYA9YAM", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["attach_idempotency_key", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "rt-toolu_01Ea6piF3ZQ4xnVeJdYA9YAM", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376439, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ea6piF3ZQ4xnVeJdYA9YAM", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 378588, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly failure and opened PR #101 against main, with alex requested as reviewer. I did not merge it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding. That gives 2.66 for 2.675, but the test expects 2.68.\n- **Fix:** Switched to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` (commit 08d3cd5986). I checked the file on the branch and it has the change.\n- **CI:** Status for ci-0001 on that commit reports **passed**. However, the `wait_for_ci` response for the same run named `main@0c0ffee000` and reported a flaky failure in `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`. I couldn't reconcile those two responses. I noted the discrepancy in the PR description. Someone should check the CI logs before merging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's expected.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NEggBiBcXaFT4wk57XvGfm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null